    "narrative": "The Austin Waves carry high expectations into today\u2019s slate, headlined by the elite 83.29 efficiency score of **Gunnar Henderson**. He is our clear standout, benefiting from a prime matchup against Holmes, G (4.75 xERA) and a significant platoon edge that makes him a must-start staple at shortstop. Joining him at the top of the board is **Drake Baldwin** (72.67), whose lead-off role against Rogers, Tr (4.59 xERA) provides maximum plate appearance potential. We are also leaning into the speed-first profile of **Nasim Nunez** (64.57) and **Jackson Merrill** (68.36); both receive moderate bumps due to the slower delivery of their opposing pitchers, which statistically enhances their stolen base probability\u2014a critical lever for our roster composition.\n\nWhile **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.87) remains a high-floor cornerstone, the decision to bench **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (55.06) was the most difficult calculation of the day. Despite the favorable park and SP matchup against Rodriguez, Ed, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** lost the tiebreaker to the superior lineup position and platoon efficiency of **Curtis Mead** and **Sam Antonacci**. Elsewhere, we are capitalizing on specific situational edges: **Andy Pages** (59.54) and **Kyle Tucker** (59.85) both carry higher floor projections than raw stats suggest, bolstered by elite BvP history against Manaea. We are keeping a close watch on **Liam Hicks** (58.77) and **Miguel Vargas** (60.12); while both are strong starts, they are hovering near the marginal threshold, and any late-breaking lineup changes could impact their daily utility. Finally, note that **Luis Robert Jr.** (50.64) remains on the bench despite the potential for stolen bases against Sasaki, as his dynamic platoon deficit and overall efficiency rating didn't justify displacing our higher-scoring outfielders today.",
